- content_for :title, "What changed and what we know is missing"
- content_for :description, "Every change to how StepsFrom measures walks and orders stays, and the known limits of the measurements."

%section.page-header
  .container
    %h1.page-header__title What changed, and what is missing
    %p.page-header__lead
      Changes to how we measure and rank, newest first, and the limits we know about. The method itself is on
      = succeed "." do
        = link_to "How we measure and rank", how_we_verify_path

.container.prose
  %h2#known-limits Known limits
  %ul
    %li
      A walk is only as good as OpenStreetMap: a footpath missing from the map can make a walk look longer than it
      is, and a stay mapped in the wrong spot is measured from there.
    %li Stays more than #{@walks.fetch(:max_access_m)} m from any mapped street have no measured walks.
    %li
      When the OpenStreetMap servers are busy, a place you searched for may show stays by straight-line distance
      until its walks are measured.
    %li Map changes reach our destinations with the weekly refresh, so a new path or stay can take up to a week to appear.
    %li Many stays have no price yet: prices come only from booking sites’ official partner programmes.

  %h2#changes Changes
  %dl.changes
    %dt
      %time{ datetime: "2026-11-04" } 4 November 2026
    %dd
      %strong Walks up to 1 km count as near.
      The limit was 2.5 km. Longer walks are no longer listed; the current limit is always on the method page.
    %dt
      %time{ datetime: "2026-11-04" } 4 November 2026
    %dd
      %strong Any place you search for is measured.
      A sight, street, venue or address we had not measured is looked up on OpenStreetMap, and the walks from the
      stays around it are measured while you wait.
    %dt
      %time{ datetime: "2026-11-03" } 3 November 2026
    %dd
      %strong Walks along the streets, from every stay to every sight.
      Walks to sights, squares, pedestrian streets, parks and beaches are measured along streets, paths and steps,
      counting busy roads to cross and flights of steps. Places can be searched for by any of their names, in any
      language.
    %dt
      %time{ datetime: "2026-11-03" } 3 November 2026
    %dd
      %strong No more hand-picked list.
      Every stay we can measure is listed automatically; we can only hide a stay, never move it up.
    %dt
      %time{ datetime: "2026-10-30" } 30 October 2026
    %dd
      %strong Stays follow OpenStreetMap.
      A stay removed from OpenStreetMap leaves the site at the next refresh.
    %dt
      %time{ datetime: "2026-10-29" } 29 October 2026
    %dd
      %strong Waterfront badges.
      Distance to the shoreline is measured from each stay’s outline, and a road or railway in between rules out
      “beachfront”.
